## Installation

The {{ spec.info.title }} CLI is a command line tool to help you interact with the {{ spec.info.title }} API. You can install it with [Homebrew](https://brew.sh), [`npm`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/{{ language.params.npmPackage }}), [Scoop](https://scoop.sh) or our install scripts, or download a [native binary](https://github.com/{{ sdk.gitUserName|url_encode }}/{{ sdk.gitRepoName|url_encode }}/releases/latest) for your operating system and architecture.

### macOS and Linux

#### Homebrew

```bash
brew install {{ language.params.homebrewTapOwner }}/{{ language.params.homebrewTapName }}/{{ language.params.executableName }}
```

Homebrew pulls the formula from the [`{{ language.params.homebrewTapOwner }}/homebrew-{{ language.params.homebrewTapName }}`](https://github.com/{{ language.params.homebrewTapOwner }}/homebrew-{{ language.params.homebrewTapName }}) tap and downloads the native binary for your platform.

#### npm

```bash
npm install -g {{ language.params.npmPackage }}
```

#### Install script

```bash
wget -q {{ sdk.url }}/cli/install.sh -O - | /bin/bash
```

### Windows

#### PowerShell

```powershell
iwr -useb {{ sdk.url }}/cli/install.ps1 | iex
```

#### Scoop

```powershell
scoop install https://raw.githubusercontent.com/{{ sdk.gitUserName }}/{{ sdk.gitRepoName|caseDash }}/master/scoop/appwrite.config.json
```

The npm package also works on Windows:

```powershell
npm install -g {{ language.params.npmPackage }}
```

### Verify the installation

```bash
{{ language.params.executableName|caseLower }} -v
```

This prints the installed version, for example `{{ sdk.version }}`.

## Shell completion

Install completion for your current shell:

```bash
{{ language.params.executableName|caseLower }} completion install
```

You can also install completion for a specific shell:

```bash
{{ language.params.executableName|caseLower }} completion install zsh
{{ language.params.executableName|caseLower }} completion install bash
{{ language.params.executableName|caseLower }} completion install fish
```

For zsh, ensure `~/.zfunc` is in your `fpath` and `compinit` is loaded from your shell config.
